Source: camera-engine-rkaiq
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Mixtile <dev@mixtile.com>
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/rockchip-linux/camera_engine_rkaiq
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 cmake,
 ninja-build,
 pkg-config,
# libdrm: rkaiq opens the DRM device to allocate buffers. Only drmOpen, not
# the auth API, which is why the patched libdrm Rockchip ships is not needed.
 libdrm-dev,
# m4 generates rkaiq/iq_parser_v2/RkAiqCalibDbTypesV2_M4.h from a .m4 template
 m4,
# xxd turns the binary IQ blob into j2s_code2bin.h. It used to come with
# vim-common and is its own package now.
 xxd

Package: camera-engine-rkaiq-rk3588
Architecture: arm64
Provides: camera-engine-rkaiq
Conflicts: camera-engine-rkaiq, camera-engine-rkaiq-rk356x
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Rockchip ISP tuning and 3A engine for RK3588
 rkaiq is the userspace half of the Rockchip ISP: it drives auto exposure,
 auto white balance and auto focus, and applies the per-sensor tuning that
 turns raw sensor output into a usable image. rkaiq_3A_server is the daemon
 that does it, and /etc/iqfiles holds the tuning.
 .
 This is the RK3588 build, ISP hardware version 30. RK3568 needs version 21
 and is a different package: the libraries are compiled against one ISP
 register layout or the other, so the two cannot be installed together.
 .
 The libraries have unversioned SONAMEs, so the bare .so symlinks are the
 ones the loader follows and the headers are here rather than in a separate
 -dev package. Nothing about that is co-installable anyway.

